    "Enrich the company at irhythmtech.com"
  ],
  "skill": "Where firmographics live:\n- Legal name, HQ, founded year: the site's about, legal, imprint or terms pages; registries (Companies House, SEC EDGAR,\n  state registries).\n- Employee count: LinkedIn company page range, or a dated statement from the company. Give the range as shown.\n- Ownership types: public (with ticker), private, PE-backed (name the firm), VC-backed, subsidiary of X.\n- Leadership: the company's team or leadership page, press releases announcing hires, LinkedIn profiles. A title is\n  current only if a recent page shows it; people move roles often, so a source older than two years needs confirmation.\n- Tech stack means tools the company uses, not tools it sells. Good evidence: job posts that list required tools,\n  integrations pages, customer case studies published by the vendor.\n- Funding: press releases, Crunchbase, investor portfolio pages. \"Total raised\" is whatever a source states; do not add up\n  rounds yourself unless the rounds are all cited.\n\nCitations and evidence:\n- source_url is one full public https URL: the page the value was read on. Never an internal file path or source id. A\n  value from two pages is two values.\n- as_of is the date the source states or was published, not today's date.\n- A value nobody published is null, listed in missing_fields. Not an estimate from memory.\n- Entity drift is the most common error: a namesake, a parent, a subsidiary or a similarly named company. Match on domain,\n  registry number, HQ city or ticker before using a page.",
